Fused the two bounds checks into a single short-circuit condition and hinted the valid path as likely, so the hot case executes one predictable branch before the table load.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    if (__builtin_expect((profile != NULL) && (profileIndex < profile->numFields), 1))
        return profile->fields[profileIndex].num;
    return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
}
```